# SPA history fallback. Every route below `/` is client-side, so a hard load of
# /profile/<id>/followers asks the host for a file that does not exist. Without
# this rule that is a 404; with it the host serves index.html and React Router
# resolves the path.
#
# Status 200, not 301: the URL must stay as typed. Never add `!` (force) - that
# would shadow the hashed JS and CSS bundles too.
#
# Vite copies public/ to the build root, so this ships as build/_redirects.
# Understood as-is by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.
/*    /index.html   200
